From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump body-parser 2.2.1 -> 2.4.0 and fast-uri 3.1.8 -> 3.1.9

Upstream: https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/commit/f7075eae3a84c3473ab4bf0a777da28db208e916
Upstream: https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/0def70338a0fa2f12a10c83ae8eafc2139ae9a07

body-parser before 2.4.0 can crash the process when a compressed request
body is followed by trailing bytes: the decompression stream has no error
listener after the body is read, so a late decoder error becomes an
uncaught exception (CVE-2026-111181). Fixed in 2.4.0.

fast-uri 3.1.8 is affected by several URI parsing/normalization issues
fixed in 3.1.9 (CVE-2026-110306, CVE-2026-110180, CVE-2026-110095,
CVE-2026-110725). Bump the Yarn resolution and lockfile accordingly.
Yarn cache regenerated and uploaded to lookaside.

